If you have to stick with `[JsonProperty]`, there is still another possible way for you avoiding to specify `MemberSerialization = MemberSerialization.OptIn` in `[JsonObject]` attributes by using a custom contract resolver that realizes the opt-in behavior.

Derive such a custom contract resolver from `DefaultContractResolver`, and all you would (probably) need to do is to override its `GetSerializableMembers` method to select only properties from a given type that are annotated with the `[JsonProperty]` attribute. It could be as basic as:
```
public class OptInContractResolver : DefaultContractResolver
{
    protected override List<MemberInfo> GetSerializableMembers(Type objectType)
    {
        return new List<MemberInfo>(
            objectType.GetProperties(BindingFlags.Instance | BindingFlags.Public | BindingFlags.FlattenHierarchy)
                .Where(m => m.IsDefined(typeof(JsonPropertyAttribute)))
        );
    }
}
```

(Depending on your specific circumstances, you might constrain this custom behavior of _GetSerializableMembers_ to your own data types.)

